SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Cabin Fever 23R
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRIDE LEADER: Jan Zerfoss\
 , average pace 12 mph.\nCue and Ride with GPS link: [Cabin Fever](https://
 ridewithgps.com/routes/40245570)\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Together
 **\n\nThis is a casual ride and the ride leader will ride at the advertise
 d pace. Some riders may ride faster than the leader so we'll likely break 
 into one or more smaller groups. We will stop to regroup periodically. Ple
 ase stay with other riders in your pace group so everyone has someone to r
 ide with and nobody is riding solo. Usually no designated sweep but nobody
  will get dropped.\n\nTerre Hill Park has well maintained restrooms that a
 re usually open. There is also a bike repair station there.\n\nPost-ride c
 offee/refreshments - we can enjoy BYO refreshments in the pavilion after t
 he ride.\n\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. Please bring water and a ba
 sic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo elimi
 nate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membershi
 p and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on\nMeetup does not mean 
 you are a club member. Join here [Member Signup](https://www.lancasterbike
 club.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\nYour RSVP is your agre
 ement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of Conduct](https://ww
 w.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=3
 23984)\n\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lanca
 sterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
